<title>RUSSIA: WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - Jan 23.</title>
<headline>WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - Jan 23.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airports of Murmansk, Arkhangelsk, Salekhard and Norilsk in northern Russia could be closed on January 23 and 24 because of strong winds, low clouds and heavy snow, the Russian Weather Service said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The probability of closure is between 80 and 90 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Flights could be postponed at airports on the Kamchatka peninsula and in Sakhalin and Magadan in Russia's Far East on January 23 and 24 because of high winds and snowstorms, the service said.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
